  "description": "Reid Viper 24 | 24 inch kids' bike\nLightweight, durable and ready for adventure – the ideal 24\" kids' bike for 8–11 year olds moving up to their first big bike.\nThe Reid Viper 24 is designed for young riders ready to take the next step on two wheels. With a lightweight 6061 alloy frame and fork, kid-specific geometry and components, it’s built to be easy to handle while giving them the freedom to explore further.\nA Shimano 7-speed drivetrain gives young riders the gears they need to tackle hills and varied terrain, while the 24 x 1.75\" tyres provide a stable, confident ride around the neighbourhood, local parks and cycle paths.\nSafety and control are built into the Viper 24, with adjustable-reach Tektro alloy V-brakes making it easy for smaller hands to brake confidently. Junior grips, a junior saddle and appropriately sized handlebars complete the rider-focused setup.\nBuilt to handle the knocks and bumps that come with growing up on two wheels, the Viper 24 is a dependable choice for everyday riding, family adventures and exploring independently.\nThe Viper 24 is ideal for:\n\n8–11 year olds ready to move up to their first big bike\n\nYoung riders developing confidence and independence on two wheels\n\nChildren moving up from a 20\" kids' bike and ready for a larger, more capable bike\n\nRiders learning to use gears, with a 7-speed drivetrain for hills and varied terrain\n\nEveryday adventures, from neighbourhood rides and trips to the park to family bike rides\n\nYoung cyclists who need a lightweight, easy-to-handle bike, with a 6061 alloy frame and fork\n\nActive kids who put their bikes through their paces, with durable components designed for everyday riding and plenty of knocks and bumps\n\nFind the right fit\nChoosing the right bike size helps your child ride comfortably, confidently and safely. Use our Kids' Bike Size Guide by clicking the tab above to find the right Reid bike based on your child’s height and age.",
